# Eval fixtures are real prompts from real work. They stay on the machine that
# made them. See test/fixtures/README.md.
test/fixtures/prompts.json
test/eval-raw.json

# No lockfile at the plugin root, deliberately.
#
# Claude Code runs `npm ci --ignore-scripts` when a plugin it installs has both
# a package.json and a lockfile. Measured: that pulls 43 MB of esbuild and
# TypeScript into every user's plugin cache, on a 60-second timeout, and not one
# byte of it is used — dist/ is bundled and the hook runs with no node_modules
# at all. Without a lockfile the install is skipped and the cache is 376 KB.
#
# Reproducibility is kept instead by pinning every devDependency to an exact
# version, and by CI failing if a fresh build of src/ differs from committed
# dist/. CI enforces that no lockfile comes back.
package-lock.json
npm-shrinkwrap.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
bun.lockb
bun.lock
